300: \]
301: Moreover \(-n\delta-3p=n(A-I)K\) and \(-3q=n(B-I)K\),
302: so the threefold comparison retains the exact integer period primitive.
303: These agree with the literal local periods and the finite-root logarithmic
304: power. The component defects, character/divisor identities, cyclic norm,
305: bounded origins and characteristic substitutions all pass in the same
306: certificate; its JSON and captured output are retained alongside the script.
307: 
308: 
309: \par\medskip\noindent\textbf{7. Exact scalar-loop witnesses and the range.}\enspace
310: 
311: For (k=1), the new parameter is the original scalar itself:
312: (lambda=w). Take the literal oriented fan basis
313: [
314:  v=(1,0),qquad w_{
315: m fan}=(-4,1),qquad
316:  det(v,w_{
317: m fan})=1,qquad delta=(0,1)=4v+w_{
318: m fan}.
319: ]
320: Thus (S=13), and the actual positive scalar loop has
321: [
322:  [Sigma_{Phi,T}]=
323: rac{(13-1)(13-3)}4=30=2pmod {28}.
324: ]
325: This example uses the shorter family itself and does not select a cube root
326: of a homotopy-sphere class.
327: 
328: The exact (k=1) range is
329: [
330:                   {0,2,6,12,14,16,20,26}.                    	ag{OS.15}
331: ]
332: For an upper bound, the formula depends on odd (S) modulo 112. Evaluating
333: those 56 residues gives exactly the set displayed. Every value is attained
334: by the following primitive physical cocharacter pairs:
335: [
336: egin{array}{c|r|r}
337:  (a,b)&S=a^2-ab+b^2&[Sigma]pmod {28}\ hline
338:  (0,1)&1&0\
339:  (1,4)&13&2\
340:  (1,3)&7&6\
341:  (3,14)&163&12\
342:  (1,6)&31&14\
343:  (2,5)&19&16\
344:  (1,10)&91&20\
345:  (3,7)&37&26
346: end{array}
347: ]
348: These are actual fan coordinates. For any displayed coprime pair choose
349: integers (r_0,s_0) with (ar_0+bs_0=1), and set
350: (v=(b,r_0)), (w_{
351: m fan}=(-a,s_0)). Then
352: (det(v,w_{
353: m fan})=1) and (av+bw_{
354: m fan}=(0,1)=delta).
355: Thus each row supplies the required actual unimodular fan, with no
356: realizability inference from an unattained residue.
357: 
358: All values for every (k) are even: with (S=2j+1), (P3K.37.3) is
359: (kj(j-1)). Conversely the fixed (S=13) fan gives (2k) modulo28.
360: As the actual cap order (m=3k) varies through the already constructed
361: positive integers, these shorter scalar families therefore realize exactly
362: the fourteen even classes. The proof of source-translation endpoint
363: minimality is retained separately with its explicit scope; it is not used
364: to infer these realized classes.
365: \end{proof}
